  "//devDependencies": {
    "eslint": "Held at 9.39.5 even though EVERY published 9.x is deprecated (\"This version is no longer supported\"). eslint 10 is not reachable from here: three of the four plugins this config loads cap their peer range at eslint 9 and have shipped nothing since — eslint-plugin-react 7.37.5 (2025-04-03, peer ^9.7), eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y 6.10.2 (peer ^9), eslint-plugin-import 2.32.0 (peer ^9). It is not a soft warning: under eslint 10, eslint-plugin-react dies with `TypeError: contextOrFilename.getFilename is not a function` because eslint 10 removed the context.getFilename() that its version detection calls. Revisit when eslint-plugin-react ships eslint 10 support; dropping the plugin instead would lose the React rules this config deliberately tunes."
  },
  "//dependencies": {
    "badwords-list": "Pinned to 2.0.1-4 deliberately. Despite the prerelease suffix, 2.0.1-4 IS the npm `latest` dist-tag (published 2024-08-18); the only non-prerelease is 1.0.0 from 2014, which is CommonJS with no type declarations and would fail `npm run typecheck`. Do not 'downgrade to a stable version'. See DEPENDENCY_AUDIT.md section 4."
